Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/opencontainers/runc v1.5.3

H-6 of the runc series: the seccomp stub gains a registration seam. With cgo
off, upstream compiles seccomp_unsupported.go, whose InitSeccomp refuses every
profile. Upstream's real filter needs libseccomp through cgo.

Ze's filter is Go code in Ze's own tree, where it is linted and tested, never
a file inside this patch. RegisterInit stores the function that builds and
loads a filter, and InitSeccomp calls it for a profile. With no function
registered a profile is still refused, as upstream does. A nil function or a
second registration panics, so nothing replaces the loader after start-up.

Enabled, FlagSupported and Version are unchanged and still answer "not
supported": they describe libseccomp, which is still absent.

No upstream pull request is opened for this change. The design is
docs/architecture/container/runtime.md.

Delete this series when Ze no longer vendors the runtime.

diff --git a/vendor/github.com/opencontainers/runc/libcontainer/seccomp/seccomp_unsupported.go b/vendor/github.com/opencontainers/runc/libcontainer/seccomp/seccomp_unsupported.go
index 25713f2327..259509a9bd 100644
--- a/vendor/github.com/opencontainers/runc/libcontainer/seccomp/seccomp_unsupported.go
+++ b/vendor/github.com/opencontainers/runc/libcontainer/seccomp/seccomp_unsupported.go
@@ -11,10 +11,31 @@ import (
 
 var ErrSeccompNotEnabled = errors.New("seccomp: config provided but seccomp not supported")
 
-// InitSeccomp does nothing because seccomp is not supported.
+// ze patch (runc-06-seccomp-seam): the filter is Go code in the tree of the
+// program that links this library, so that it is linted and tested there.
+// That code registers its loader here, and InitSeccomp calls it.
+var registeredInit func(config *configs.Seccomp) (int, error)
+
+// RegisterInit registers the function InitSeccomp calls to build and load the
+// filter of a profile. Like InitSeccomp it answers the seccomp notify
+// descriptor, or -1 when the profile needs none. It MUST be called from a
+// package init function, once: a nil function or a second registration is a
+// programming error and panics, so nothing replaces a filter loader later.
+func RegisterInit(load func(config *configs.Seccomp) (int, error)) {
+	if load == nil || registeredInit != nil {
+		panic("seccomp: RegisterInit needs one non-nil function, registered once")
+	}
+	registeredInit = load
+}
+
+// InitSeccomp loads the filter of config through the registered function. It
+// refuses a profile when no function is registered.
 func InitSeccomp(config *configs.Seccomp) (int, error) {
 	if config != nil {
-		return -1, ErrSeccompNotEnabled
+		if registeredInit == nil {
+			return -1, ErrSeccompNotEnabled
+		}
+		return registeredInit(config)
 	}
 	return -1, nil
 }
